{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'MC08|MC09|MC10|MC11|MC12|MC18|MC26' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md; rg -n 'reconstruct|Rounding|rounding|uncertainty|aggregation|Incomplete|Unknown|bound' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md | head -55; cat docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc\"","aggregated_output":"67:| MC08 | Preserve jointly consistent discrete alternatives and continuous unknowns across accounts, notes and dates. U2, D. | Define history-family and choice/constraint semantics; provide cases preserving linked alternatives and rejecting incompatible combinations without independent account-by-account selection. | Specified shared symbols, choices and joint formulas in Chs. 2, 6–8. Exact reference checks retain fixed/floating histories, reject incompatible debt and reject incompatible marginal extrema. General reconstruction implementation remains pending. G1, G2, G15. |\n68:| MC09 | Construct historical families through a specified method, with honest scope and search completeness. U2, U3, D. | Define candidate templates, model-scope records, instantiation and constraint lowering, feasible/infeasible/unknown results, truncation and coverage evidence. | Specified finite template/slot construction and coverage rules in Ch. 6/Core 0. Northstar bridges are solved and checked within the declared scope; completeness concerns that model only. A compiler for arbitrary supported template registries remains pending. G1, G3. |\n69:| MC10 | Distinguish uncertainty about facts, disclosure readings, admissible accounting treatment, estimates, behaviour and future shocks. U2, P, D. | Specify the categories, dependencies and admissibility checks; show why a factual unknown, permitted election and unsupported treatment cannot be substituted for one another. | Specified six uncertainty kinds with separate admission/provenance/dependency rules in Core 0 and Chs. 6–8. Examples distinguish factual composition, permitted inventory election and unsupported treatment. Factual/assumption admission is now tested for the authored debt case; all-category semantic validation remains pending. G6, G15. |\n70:| MC11 | Preserve the economic memory and scenario responses needed when histories are aggregated or refined. U2, D. | Define required state by contract/lot/cohort, permitted grouping transformations, supported horizon/scenarios, exact versus approximate status and invalidation when the query changes. | Specified grouping keys, additive transition/report proof, exact/approximate status and query invalidation in Ch. 6/Core 0. Debt, lot and cohort counterexamples are given; a general equivalence checker or empirical approximate-cohort error bound is not established. G1, G16. |\n71:| MC12 | Add probabilities only under an explicit justified joint measure, and retain unweighted alternatives when weights are unsupported. U2, P, D. | Specify optional weight/prior/likelihood records, dependence, overlaps, updates and mass preservation; provide a worked weighted and unweighted example with clear interpretation. | Specified finite joint weighting and one-use likelihood update in Ch. 6/Core 0; exact posterior 3/11 and 8/11, mixture and retained unresolved mass are checked. Continuous inference requires a target-specific method and validation. G2, G6, G15. |\n82:| MC18 | Preserve joint conditional future outcomes, honest bounds and distinct failure/completeness states. U2, P, D. | Define result payloads and queries that retain branch/path dependence, distinguish sampled ranges from certified bounds and distinguish default from unsupported/numerically failed output without silent dropping or renormalisation. | Specified result cells, branch statuses, strict bound attainment and unresolved mass in Chs. 6, 8, 10/Core 0. Exact linear, joint-output and funding/default reference checks pass; general simulation/result-query implementation remains pending. G2, G3, G6. |\n100:| MC26 | Specify supported numerical/solver operations and their limits. U3, P, D. | Define formula fragments, reformulations, exact/approximate monetary treatment, rounding, strict-domain bounds, infeasibility/conflict evidence, timeout and resource behaviour. | Specified rational-linear/finite-choice scope, amount reformulation, quantisation distinctions and typed unknowns in Ch. 6/Core 0. Z3 checks 4.975 attained and 7.035 unattained and concrete histories. Nonlinear solvers and a production rounding/optimization layer remain pending. G3, G10. |\n11:bounded static admission for that profile, including references, source-reading\n67:embedded as top-level IR nodes. The frozen demonstration registry and bounded\n76:does not pretend to be an original page bounding box. Monetary Context has\n91:Source symbol-domain intervals are closed; strict bounds use explicit\n93:surface syntax has no unbounded loops, recursion, dynamic code evaluation or\n120:precision is a domain, not a tolerance argument. Unknown rounding convention\n124:available; `rounding_rule` identifies the declared convention or is null for\n126:An exact numeric domain has equal closed bounds; an interval has ordered bounds\n127:and explicit endpoint inclusion (a null endpoint is unbounded and open).\n128:Finite-domain `values` are distinct typed expression IDs and use null bounds.\n129:A missing domain has null bounds, no values, and a non-null `missing_reason`;\n132:an unknown rounding convention.\n144:| roundMoney | Money<C>, Int, String -> Money<C>; only half_even supported in DemoDebt; rounding at posting boundary, rational ties exact |\n159:timing/calendar resolution, allowed choices, bounds, and forbidden/unsupported\n178:bounds, finite enums and Boolean combinations lowered to finite disjunctions.\n180:minor-unit variables with a separately declared bounded integer solver. Integer\n182:Unknown-by-unknown products, symbolic discount rates/exponents, arbitrary\n183:functions and unbounded integer search return UnsupportedFragment/Unknown.\n190:attainment flags, proof/certificate reference, rounding stage and scope. Strict\n191:inequalities require infimum/supremum semantics. An unbounded result is neither\n209:the end-of-day boundary. Cumulative subtraction requires same start, nested\n260:NumericalFailure, SolverUnknown, Cancelled. Default retains the legal obligations\n316:## APIs and adapter boundaries\n328:| reconstruct | IR, ModelScope, view, solver_lock, budgets | HistoryFamily and cell coverage, witnesses/conflicts/unknowns |\n331:| bound | formula, query expression, domain, quantisation mode, solver/budget | certified bound/attainment or explicit Unknown/Unbounded |\n346:provides layout/table proposals with page bounds and conversion status; a table\n366:The following are expected exchanges at the AccDSL boundary, not captured\n376:  metadata is retained separately from that nominal value. An uncertainty\n377:  interval additionally needs the declared rounding convention; scale alone\n393:  This is an ACTUS-oriented boundary example; an actual ACTUS service request\nmodule BorrowingExample version \"1\";\nuse DemoDebt version \"1\";\nsource note7 = external(\"synthetic-note-7\");\nentity Acme functional USD;\nbook Local entity Acme basis DemoDebt version \"1\";\naccount Cash : Asset book Local;\naccount Debt : Liability book Local;\naccount InterestExpense : Expense book Local;\naccount Retained : Equity book Local;\nopening after2025 for Local from external(\"after-2025-close\");\nobservation debt : Money<USD> instant @2025-12-31 = 100 USD from note7;\nsymbol alpha : Real in [0, 1] because \"Fixed-rate proportion not disclosed\";\ncontract loans : DebtMix book Local {\n  principal = value(debt);\n  fixed_fraction = alpha;\n  fixed_rate = 0.05 per year;\n  initial_floating_rate = 0.05 per year;\n}\nalternative allFixed { assume alpha == 1; }\nalternative allFloating { assume alpha == 0; }\nscenario rateShock { set market_rate = constant(0.07 per year); }\nreport statements for Local { mapping = external(\"DemoDebt.statements.v1\"); }\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,95p' AGENTS.md; rg -n '\"'^def |''^class |alternative|choice_group|constraint|family'\"' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py | tail -85\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,95p' AGENTS.md; rg -n '\"'^def |''^class |alternative|choice_group|constraint|family'\"' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py | tail -85\"","aggregated_output":"# AccDSL project instructions\n\n## Mission entry point\n\nBefore substantive work in this project, read:\n\n1. [Mission control](MISSION_CONTROL.md).\n2. [Requirements and acceptance evidence](docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md).\n3. [Current checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md).\n4. The gap records relevant to the task:\n   [initial audit](docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md) and\n   [expanded mission audit](docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md).\n5. For the authorised master-program work, read the\n   [master checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md), executable\n   phase catalog and current `data/accounting-master/next-plan.md`. The older\n   corpus checkpoint remains historical evidence; current phase execution is\n   recorded by the master without rewriting frozen release hashes.\n\nThe mission preserves the user's goals across sessions. Current user directions\nand higher-priority instructions still control. Local documents must not be\nused to request fresh permission for work already authorised by the user.\n\n## Working rules\n\n- Identify the MC requirements addressed by each nontrivial plan or work unit.\n  Audit the plan before implementation, experiments or long diagnostics.\n- Preserve the full goals while staging execution. A small financing demo,\n  clean PDF build or six populated research ledgers cannot close requirements\n  for whole-company representation, research quality or implementation detail.\n- Distinguish direct user requirements, policy requirements and derived\n  engineering choices. Do not silently convert a convenient library, model\n  assumption or stage boundary into an immutable product requirement.\n- Keep source evidence, interpretations, assumptions, joint history families\n  and scenario-specific results separate and traceable. Preserve unknowns;\n  do not invent facts, probabilities, accounting compliance or completeness.\n- Close gaps with the specified evidence, and update the requirements register\n  and checkpoint after meaningful changes. Add newly discovered gaps rather\n  than treating the current list as exhaustive.\n- Follow the applicable policies under\n  `/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies`. Preserve unrelated work and the\n  original paper collection. The existing `.git` marker is not a usable\n  repository; do not initialise or commit merely to create provenance.\n- Keep operational mission/checklist material out of the reader-facing\n  scholarly narrative unless it serves a real implementation-reference purpose.\n- Apply MC35, the user's internal-preparation-before-paid-review requirement.\n  Finish feasible source research, facts, calculations, software checks and\n  document repairs before referring a specific question to a professional.\n  Supply a proposed answer, exact sources, competing interpretation and checked\n  consequences. Keep unfinished internal work on the internal queue; “human\n  review pending” is an acceptance status, not a reason to stop that work.\n  Ordinary reader feedback need not be purchased from an accounting firm.\n  No professional engagement, outreach or fees are authorised by this policy.\n  See `docs/design/review/internal-before-expert.md` and the current checkpoint.\n\nThe current manuscript is specification-incomplete. Read the checkpoint and\nrequirements before resuming from an older note that says only final review\nremains. This file authorises no autonomous background campaign or external\npublication; it directs work undertaken under the user's active instructions.\n1392:                cid = f\"constraint:{_clean_id(alt.name)}:{index}\"\n1393:                self.ir[\"constraints\"].append({\"id\": cid, \"expression\": eid, \"kind\": \"assumption\",\n1395:                alt_constraints.append(cid)\n1396:                self._assumption_row(f\"alternative:{alt.name}:{index}\", eid, alt.name, evidence)\n1397:            if not alt_constraints:\n1398:                self.fail(\"MissingAlternativeCondition\", \"named alternatives require a Boolean condition\", alt.name)\n1399:            self.ir[\"alternatives\"].append({\n1403:                \"constraints\": alt_constraints, \"choice_group\": None,\n1407:        for con in self.constraints.values():\n1408:            eid = self.lower_expr(con.expression, f\"constraint:{con.name}\", \"condition\")[0]\n1409:            self.ir[\"constraints\"].append({\"id\": con.name, \"expression\": eid, \"kind\": \"assumption\",\n1411:            constraint_ids.append(con.name)\n1412:            self._assumption_row(f\"constraint:{con.name}\", eid, model_scope, evidence)\n1451:        # Profile scope and conservative family status.  This profile does not\n1459:        family_id = f\"history:{_clean_id(self.model_id)}\"\n1460:        self.ir[\"historyFamilies\"].append({\"id\": family_id, \"scope\": model_scope,\n1462:            \"symbols\": list(self.symbols), \"choices\": [], \"constraints\": constraint_ids,\n1463:            \"alternatives\": alt_ids, \"feasibility\": \"Unknown\", \"coverage\": \"PartialSearch\",\n1479:        self.ir[\"constraints\"].sort(key=lambda r: r[\"id\"])\n1480:        self.ir[\"alternatives\"].sort(key=lambda r: r[\"id\"])\n1505:        if key.startswith(\"alternative:\"):\n1506:            meta = self.bindings.assumption(\"alternative\")\n1511:        elif key.startswith(\"constraint:\"):\n1512:            meta = self.bindings.assumption(\"constraint\")\n1528:def _numeric_type(typ: str) -> bool:\n1532:def _is_scalar(typ: str) -> bool:\n1536:def _merge_context(left: Optional[str], right: Optional[str], owner: str, compiler: _Compiler) -> Optional[str]:\n1542:def _literal_value(expr: Expr, where: str) -> Any:\n1550:def _arithmetic(op: str, left: Any, right: Any) -> Any:\n1564:def _compare(op: str, left: Any, right: Any) -> Optional[bool]:\n1571:def _fold_bool(op: str, left: Any, right: Any) -> Optional[bool]:\n1577:def compile_program(program: Program, bindings: CompileBindings,\n1598:def _load_schema() -> dict[str, Any]:\n1605:def _invalid(code: str, message: str, location: str) -> Diagnostic:\n1609:def _nodes(ir: Mapping[str, Any]) -> tuple[dict[str, tuple[str, Mapping[str, Any]]], Optional[Diagnostic]]:\n1624:def _ref(nodes: Mapping[str, tuple[str, Mapping[str, Any]]], identifier: str,\n1633:class _IRTypeChecker:\n1770:def _expression_bounds(identifier, nodes):\n1793:def validate_ir(ir: Mapping[str, Any], bindings: CompileBindings,\n1938:            if row[\"scope\"] not in model_ids | scope_ids and row[\"scope\"] not in {a[\"id\"] for a in ir[\"alternatives\"]} and row[\"scope\"] not in {c[\"id\"] for c in ir[\"contracts\"]} and row[\"scope\"] not in {s[\"id\"] for s in ir[\"scenarios\"]}:\n1948:            if aid.startswith(\"assumption:alternative_\"):\n1949:                key = \"alternative\"\n1954:            elif aid.startswith(\"assumption:constraint_\"):\n1955:                key = \"constraint\"\n1967:        for row in ir[\"constraints\"]:\n1970:                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"ConstraintType\", \"constraint expression must be Boolean\", row[\"id\"]))\n1997:        alternatives = {r[\"id\"]: r for r in ir[\"alternatives\"]}\n1998:        for row in ir[\"alternatives\"]:\n2000:                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"AlternativeScope\", \"alternative parent or scope is unknown\", row[\"id\"]))\n2001:            meta = next((a for a in bindings.alternatives if a.name == row[\"id\"]), None)\n2003:                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"AlternativeMetadata\", \"alternative metadata differs from binding\", row[\"id\"]))\n2004:            if not row[\"constraints\"]:\n2005:                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"MissingAlternativeCondition\", \"alternative requires at least one condition\", row[\"id\"]))\n2006:            for cid in row[\"constraints\"]:\n2007:                c = next((x for x in ir[\"constraints\"] if x[\"id\"] == cid), None)\n2009:                    raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"AlternativeScope\", \"alternative condition is not scoped to its branch\", row[\"id\"]))\n2031:                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"MissingWitness\", \"feasible family requires a witness\", row[\"id\"]))\n2035:                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"CoverageClaim\", \"Core0.1 family must remain explicitly unsearched\", row[\"id\"]))\n2036:            expected_constraints = {c[\"id\"] for c in ir[\"constraints\"] if c[\"scope\"] == row[\"scope\"]}\n2037:            if set(row[\"constraints\"]) != expected_constraints or row[\"witnesses\"] or row[\"solver_results\"]:\n2038:                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"FamilyMembership\", \"family must retain global constraints without invented search evidence\", row[\"id\"]))\n2039:            if set(row[\"symbols\"]) != {s[\"id\"] for s in ir[\"symbols\"]} or set(row[\"alternatives\"]) != set(alternatives):\n2040:                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"FamilyMembership\", \"family must retain all shared symbols and alternatives\", row[\"id\"]))\n2042:                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"FamilyMembership\", \"family evidence/opening references are unknown\", row[\"id\"]))\n2076:def _validate_profile_integrity(ir, bindings, nodes, checker):\n2089:    model, scope, family = ir[\"models\"][0], ir[\"modelScopes\"][0], ir[\"historyFamilies\"][0]\n2090:    if (model[\"scope\"] != scope[\"id\"] or family[\"scope\"] != scope[\"id\"] or\n2096:                \"symbols\", \"contracts\", \"alternatives\", \"scenarios\", \"reportMappings\") for r in ir[k]}\n2106:    if family[\"choices\"]:\n2107:        raise _diag(\"UnsupportedProfile\", \"finite choices are outside Core0.1\", family[\"id\"])\n2108:    alternatives = {r[\"id\"]: r for r in ir[\"alternatives\"]}\n2109:    if not alternatives:\n2110:        raise _diag(\"ProfileCardinality\", \"at least one alternative is required\", \"alternatives\")\n2112:    for row in ir[\"constraints\"]:\n2113:        if row[\"scope\"] not in set(alternatives) | {scope[\"id\"]} or row[\"kind\"] != \"assumption\":\n2114:            raise _diag(\"ConstraintScope\", \"constraint has unsupported scope or kind\", row[\"id\"])\n2116:    for alt in alternatives.values():\n2117:        expected = {c[\"id\"] for c in ir[\"constraints\"] if c[\"scope\"] == alt[\"id\"]}\n2118:        if set(alt[\"constraints\"]) != expected or len(alt[\"constraints\"]) != len(expected):\n2134:        key = (\"alternative\" if row[\"scope\"] in alternatives else\n2135:               \"constraint\" if row[\"scope\"] == scope[\"id\"] else\n2144:class _Symbolic:\n2148:def evaluate_expression(ir: Mapping[str, Any], identifier: str,\n2201:def semantic_projection(ir: Mapping[str, Any] | None) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n2205:    # source context, package locks, assumptions, alternatives and bindings.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '105,198p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; sed -n '275,315p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; sed -n '1300,1425p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '105,198p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; sed -n '275,315p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; sed -n '1300,1425p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py\"","aggregated_output":"## Exact values, contexts and built-ins\n\nRationals use base-10 signed numerator strings and positive denominator strings,\nlowest terms; zero is `0/1`. Money adds only within one currency and compatible\ncontext. Real times money is money; rate times money must also supply a\nYearFraction through `simpleInterest`. Rate alone is not a dimensionless Real.\nNo rate basis is implicitly coerced. The demonstration's accrual rule uses\n`simpleInterest(principal,rate,fraction)` explicitly. Integer counts stay integer.\nDivision by a symbolic value\nrequires nonzero proof and is outside the rational-linear solver fragment.\n\nContext equality compares entity, perimeter version, measurement basis,\ncurrency/unit, instant/period/calendar and dimensions. A sum may discard a\ndimension only through a valid partition mapping. Reference fields and source\nspans may differ without changing financial comparability. Observation\nprecision is a domain, not a tolerance argument. Unknown rounding convention\nis an unresolved reading, not an assumed half-unit interval.\n\nDomain `display` preserves the disclosed spelling, unit/scale and sign when\navailable; `rounding_rule` identifies the declared convention or is null for\nan unrounded mathematical symbol. The SourceSpan retains the original text.\nAn exact numeric domain has equal closed bounds; an interval has ordered bounds\nand explicit endpoint inclusion (a null endpoint is unbounded and open).\nFinite-domain `values` are distinct typed expression IDs and use null bounds.\nA missing domain has null bounds, no values, and a non-null `missing_reason`;\nother domain kinds have null `missing_reason`. Empty or contradictory admitted\ndomains return an explicit consistency error. Display text alone never supplies\nan unknown rounding convention.\n\nThe complete built-in set is:\n\n| Name | Signature and effect |\n| --- | --- |\n| external | String -> SourceRef; resolves a frozen registry key; never fetches network content during evaluation |\n| value | Observation<T> -> contextual T or shared constrained Symbol<T>; missing raises MissingEvidence |\n| constant | T -> dated exogenous Driver<T>, all dates in the explicit scenario horizon |\n| simpleInterest | Money<C>, Rate<annual_simple>, YearFraction -> Money<C>, exact product; symbolic classification happens after expansion |\n| yearFraction | start, end, CalendarRef, ConventionRef -> YearFraction; supported conventions `one_year` and `half_year_fixture` require exact named periods; others require a registered calculator |\n| currencyScale | CurrencyRef -> Int from the frozen currency registry, USD=2 in demonstration |\n| roundMoney | Money<C>, Int, String -> Money<C>; only half_even supported in DemoDebt; rounding at posting boundary, rational ties exact |\n| sumOver | PartitionRef, array of contextual T -> contextual T with that dimension removed; disjoint/exhaustive population proof required |\n| convert | Money<C1>, Measurement<Rate<C2/C1>> -> Money<C2>; valuation date and purpose must match, source amount retained |\n| balance | StateRef, AccountRef -> signed Money<C>; read-only committed state at information date |\n\nAll other functions must have a package-registered pure signature and versioned\nimplementation digest; their capability is explicit. Rules may bind values,\ncheck requirements and propose postings. They cannot sample, mutate state or\naccess I/O. Contract and behaviour plugins produce proposed events/state\nchanges through the typed interfaces below. Zero-posting contract changes need\nan explicit non-recognition operation.\n\n## Reconstruction model and finite coverage\n\nA ModelScope lists templates, slots per entity/period, books, account roles,\ntiming/calendar resolution, allowed choices, bounds, and forbidden/unsupported\noperations. A slot is a possible aggregate event, with an active flag and\nnonnegative amount; inactive implies zero. A template declares both its posting\nincidence vector and economic-state change. Sales and collections are different\nslots; issue and reset are different slots. Debt states retain F/V, rates,\nreset calendar, maturity and hedge links even when historical incidence agrees.\n\nInstantiate every declared slot once, then share variables by economic IDs and\nobservation IDs. Compile roll-forwards and report mappings into constraints;\nadd each accepted evidence domain once. Match source observations by exact\ncontext/mapping, never by label similarity. Attach source/assumption IDs to\nconstraints. Branch on finite choices only, with mutually exclusive guards;\ncontinuous families remain formulas. Count completed, infeasible and unresolved\nchoice cells. `ExactWithinScope` requires every cell decided and each matching\nsource obligation resolved or explicitly outside simulation scope. A satisfied\nwitness alone does not establish coverage. Real-world completeness is never\ninferred from this finite result.\n\nSupported solver fragment: rational linear equalities/inequalities, strict\nbounds, finite enums and Boolean combinations lowered to finite disjunctions.\nMoney quantisation either occurs after continuous analysis or uses integer\nminor-unit variables with a separately declared bounded integer solver. Integer\nand nonlinear constraints may not be silently submitted as continuous LPs.\nUnknown-by-unknown products, symbolic discount rates/exponents, arbitrary\nfunctions and unbounded integer search return UnsupportedFragment/Unknown.\nFixed proportions times known totals are linear; variable F,V with F+V=D is\nlinear even when D is rounded. A fixed constraint F/D >= a with known a and\nproved D>0 becomes F>=aD; an unknown a restores bilinearity.\n\nFeasibility results are sat+exact witness, unsat+constraint/source core or\nunknown+reason+undecided formula. Bounds include lower/upper rational value,\nattainment flags, proof/certificate reference, rounding stage and scope. Strict\ninequalities require infimum/supremum semantics. An unbounded result is neither\nunknown nor a finite extreme. Resource budgets are explicit request fields;\ntimeout preserves undecided cells rather than deleting them.\n\n## Temporal selection and local review\n\nAn EvidenceView first filters by availability cutoff and (if requested)\ningestion cutoff. Day-only availability maps to the next local midnight using\n## Identity, replay, migration and storage\n\nCanonical bytes are UTF-8 JSON, NFC strings, sorted ASCII keys, separators `,`/`:`\nwithout whitespace, no floats, NaN, duplicate keys or negative zero. All numeric\nvalues are reduced rational records. Arrays preserve order except schema fields\ndeclared sets: dependencies, source IDs and constraint conjunctions sort by ID.\nNo general algebraic equivalence rewriting is implied. Evidence identity hashes\nraw documents, locators, extraction/review versions and context. Model identity\nhashes normalised IR, assumptions, rule/calculator locks and resolution contract,\nexcluding source byte offsets/formatting. Run identity additionally hashes\nevidence view, scenarios, horizon, outputs, numeric/calendars, stream scheme and\nenvironment profile. Every digest is SHA-256 with a domain/version prefix.\n\nEvent ID hashes run-independent economic owner, schedule version, date, phase,\noperation and occurrence ordinal. Idempotency keys pair run ID and event ID;\nsame payload returns the committed result, changed payload yields conflict.\nIndependent events may reorder only if their read/write sets are disjoint or\nthe package proves commutation, including cash/funding constraints. Otherwise\nexplicit dependencies decide order or expose ambiguity. Atomic commit includes\neconomic state, journals, measurements and explanation edges.\n\nThe reference random primitive hashes the canonical tuple (stream-v1, seed,\ncoupling-group, entity, contract/cohort, economic-date, shock-kind, draw-index),\ntakes the first unsigned 64 bits in big-endian order, and maps to the open-unit\nrational (integer+1/2)/2^64. Branch enumeration order is absent. Coupling groups\ndeclare shared uniforms; marginal transforms and correlation construction are\nversioned. This is a deterministic reference primitive, not a claim of validated\nMonte Carlo quality. Research runs must name an assessed counter-based generator\nand preserve the same keying contract. Gaussian/transcendental transforms require\na numerical environment and comparison tolerance; rational examples are exact.\n\nSQLite owns immutable source/readings/review rows and transactional execution\nmetadata; content-addressed files own raw bytes and frozen JSON; DuckDB reads\nversioned Parquet exports for analytics. No independent mutable copy owns truth.\nForeign keys must resolve before commit. Schema migration is original payload +\nnew payload + mapping + before/after IDs. Representation-only migration needs\nconformance equivalence on the supported node set; changed semantics creates a\nnew model. A major version is never relabelled as compatible merely because its\nJSON parses. Restart requires exact locked identities and the last committed\nstate; changed inputs require a new run.\n\n        observation_contexts: dict[str, str] = {}\n        for obs in self.observations.values():\n            _iso(obs.instant, obs.name)\n            if not obs.type_name.startswith(\"Money<\"):\n                self.fail(\"UnsupportedObservationType\", \"Core0.1 observations are monetary\", obs.name)\n            currency = obs.type_name[6:-1]\n            if currency != entity.currency:\n                self.fail(\"ContextMismatch\", \"observation currency must match the entity currency\", obs.name)\n            key = source_keys.get(obs.source)\n            if key is None:\n                self.fail(\"UnknownReference\", f\"observation source {obs.source!r} is not a source alias\", obs.name)\n            reading = self.bindings.reading(key)\n            oi = self.lower_expr(obs.value, f\"observation:{obs.name}\", \"value\", obs.type_name)\n            if oi[1] != obs.type_name:\n                self.fail(\"TypeMismatch\", \"observation literal must carry matching currency\", obs.name)\n            if _fraction(_literal_value(obs.value, obs.name)) != reading.amount:\n                self.fail(\"SourceReadingMismatch\", \"surface observation and bound reading disagree\", obs.name)\n            if reading.currency != currency or reading.instant != obs.instant:\n                self.fail(\"ReadingContextMismatch\", \"bound reading does not match observation context\", obs.name)\n            context_id = f\"context:{_clean_id(obs.name)}\"\n            observation_contexts[obs.name] = context_id\n            self.ir[\"contexts\"].append({\n                \"id\": context_id, \"entity\": entity.name, \"perimeter\": self.bindings.entity_perimeter,\n                \"concept\": \"debt_principal\", \"basis\": package.id, \"measurement\": \"principal\",\n                \"time\": _time(\"instant\", obs.instant, None, self.bindings.calendar_id),\n                \"unit\": currency, \"currency\": currency, \"taxonomy_version\": None, \"dimensions\": [],\n            })\n            document_id, span_id, view_id = evidence[key]\n            reading_id = self._reading_ids[key]\n            review_id = f\"review:{_clean_id(key)}\"\n            self.ir[\"observations\"].append({\n                \"id\": obs.name, \"context\": context_id, \"domain\": {\n                    \"kind\": \"exact\", \"lower\": rational(reading.amount), \"upper\": rational(reading.amount),\n                    \"lower_closed\": True, \"upper_closed\": True, \"values\": [], \"missing_reason\": None,\n                    \"display\": obs.value.display or f\"{reading.amount} {currency}\",\n                    \"rounding_rule\": \"exact_binding\",\n                }, \"source_spans\": [span_id], \"reading\": reading_id,\n                \"review_decision\": review_id, \"supersedes\": [], \"revision_group\": f\"binding-{_clean_id(key)}\",\n            })\n            for view in self.ir[\"evidenceViews\"]:\n                if view[\"id\"] == view_id:\n                    view[\"observations\"].append(obs.name)\n        # Symbols and declarations.\n        for symbol in self.symbols.values():\n            if symbol.type_name != \"Real\":\n                self.fail(\"UnsupportedSymbol\", \"Core0.1 admits one Real interval symbol\", symbol.name)\n            low = self.lower_expr(symbol.lower, f\"symbol:{symbol.name}\", \"lower\", \"Real\")\n            high = self.lower_expr(symbol.upper, f\"symbol:{symbol.name}\", \"upper\", \"Real\")\n            if low[1] != \"Real\" or high[1] != \"Real\" or low[3] is None or high[3] is None or low[3] > high[3]:\n                self.fail(\"InvalidDomain\", \"symbol bounds must be ordered constants\", symbol.name)\n            source_key = next(iter(source_keys.values()))\n            admission = self.bindings.admission(symbol.name)\n            if admission.reading_key != source_key or _string(admission.reason) != _string(symbol.reason):\n                self.fail(\"SymbolAdmission\", \"source reason and supplied admission disagree\", symbol.name)\n            span_id = evidence[source_key][1]\n            self.ir[\"symbols\"].append({\n                \"id\": symbol.name, \"type\": symbol.type_name, \"context\": None,\n                \"domain\": {\"kind\": \"interval\", \"lower\": rational(low[3]), \"upper\": rational(high[3]),\n                            \"lower_closed\": True, \"upper_closed\": True, \"values\": [],\n                            \"missing_reason\": None, \"display\": None, \"rounding_rule\": None},\n                \"uncertainty_kind\": self.bindings.symbol_uncertainty, \"scope\": self.model_id,\n                \"dependencies\": [], \"admission\": f\"admission:{symbol.name}\", \"provenance\": [span_id],\n            })\n        for name in self.lets:\n            self._lower_let(name)\n        # Contract, alternatives, and scenario expressions.\n        contract = next(iter(self.contracts.values()))\n        fields = dict(contract.fields)\n        required_fields = {\"principal\", \"fixed_fraction\", \"fixed_rate\", \"initial_floating_rate\"}\n        if set(fields) != required_fields:\n            self.fail(\"ContractFields\", \"DebtMix requires principal, fraction and two rates\", contract.name)\n        field_rows = []\n        for name in (\"principal\", \"fixed_fraction\", \"fixed_rate\", \"initial_floating_rate\"):\n            expected = {\"principal\": f\"Money<{entity.currency}>\", \"fixed_fraction\": \"Real\",\n                        \"fixed_rate\": \"Rate<annual_simple>\", \"initial_floating_rate\": \"Rate<annual_simple>\"}[name]\n            info = self.lower_expr(fields[name], f\"contract:{contract.name}\", f\"field:{name}\", expected)\n            if info[1] != expected:\n                self.fail(\"ContractType\", f\"field {name!r} has type {info[1]}, expected {expected}\", contract.name)\n            if name in {\"fixed_rate\", \"initial_floating_rate\"}:\n                self._assumption_row(f\"contract:{contract.name}:{name}\", info[0], contract.name, evidence)\n            field_rows.append({\"name\": name, \"expression\": info[0]})\n        self.ir[\"contracts\"].append({\"id\": contract.name, \"type\": f\"{package.id}/{contract.type_name}\",\n                                      \"book\": contract.book, \"fields\": field_rows, \"package\": package.id,\n                                      \"source_refs\": [evidence[next(iter(source_keys.values()))][1]]})\n        alt_ids = []\n        constraint_ids = []\n        for alt in self.alternatives.values():\n            meta = self.bindings.alternative(alt.name)\n            alt_ids.append(alt.name)\n            alt_constraints = []\n            for index, assumption in enumerate(alt.assumptions):\n                eid = self.lower_expr(assumption, f\"alternative:{alt.name}\", f\"assumption:{index}\")[0]\n                cid = f\"constraint:{_clean_id(alt.name)}:{index}\"\n                self.ir[\"constraints\"].append({\"id\": cid, \"expression\": eid, \"kind\": \"assumption\",\n                                                \"scope\": alt.name, \"source_refs\": []})\n                alt_constraints.append(cid)\n                self._assumption_row(f\"alternative:{alt.name}:{index}\", eid, alt.name, evidence)\n            if not alt_constraints:\n                self.fail(\"MissingAlternativeCondition\", \"named alternatives require a Boolean condition\", alt.name)\n            self.ir[\"alternatives\"].append({\n                \"id\": alt.name, \"parent\": f\"history:{_clean_id(self.model_id)}\", \"scope\": model_scope,\n                \"author\": meta.author,\n                \"created_at\": meta.created_at,\n                \"constraints\": alt_constraints, \"choice_group\": None,\n                \"reason\": meta.reason, \"evidence\": [evidence[next(iter(source_keys.values()))][1]],\n                \"opposing_evidence\": [],\n            })\n        for con in self.constraints.values():\n            eid = self.lower_expr(con.expression, f\"constraint:{con.name}\", \"condition\")[0]\n            self.ir[\"constraints\"].append({\"id\": con.name, \"expression\": eid, \"kind\": \"assumption\",\n                                           \"scope\": model_scope, \"source_refs\": []})\n            constraint_ids.append(con.name)\n            self._assumption_row(f\"constraint:{con.name}\", eid, model_scope, evidence)\n        scenario = next(iter(self.scenarios.values()))\n        settings = dict(scenario.settings)\n        if set(settings) != {\"market_rate\"}:\n            self.fail(\"ScenarioFields\", \"Core0.1 scenario requires one market_rate setting\", scenario.name)\n        driver = self.lower_expr(settings[\"market_rate\"], f\"scenario:{scenario.name}\", \"market_rate\")\n        if not driver[1].startswith(\"Driver<Rate<\"):\n            self.fail(\"ScenarioType\", \"market_rate must be a constant annual rate driver\", scenario.name)\n        self._assumption_row(f\"scenario:{scenario.name}\", driver[0], scenario.name, evidence)\n        self.ir[\"scenarios\"].append({\"id\": scenario.name, \"kind\": \"ExogenousStress\",\n                                      \"drivers\": [{\"name\": \"market_rate\", \"expression\": driver[0]}],\n                                      \"probability_model\": None, \"observed_event\": None, \"structural_model\": None,\n                                      \"replaced_equations\": [], \"visibility\": \"announced\"})\n        # Opening state and report mapping.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^def |inventory|protected|manifest|OBSERVATIONS'\"' scripts/check_accounting_p03.py; sed -n '1,90p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py; rg -n 'def compile|def validate|def _expr|def expression|class Compile' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py scripts/core0_frontends_v1.py; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib,json\np=pathlib.Path('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P04')\nprint('Structured inventories', [str(q) for q in p.rglob('*inventory*')]); d=json.loads((p/'phase-entry-inventory.json').read_text()); print('Inventory count',len(d));print('Example',list(d.items())[:2])\nfor name in ['borrowings','northstar']:\n d=json.loads(pathlib.Path('docs/design/fixtures/'+name+'.json').read_text());print(name, list(d));print(str(d)[:1300])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^def |inventory|protected|manifest|OBSERVATIONS'\"' scripts/check_accounting_p03.py; sed -n '1,90p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py; rg -n 'def compile|def validate|def _expr|def expression|class Compile' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py scripts/core0_frontends_v1.py; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib,json\np=pathlib.Path('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P04')\nprint('Structured inventories', [str(q) for q in p.rglob('*inventory*')]); d=json.loads((p/'phase-entry-inventory.json').read_text()); print('Inventory count',len(d));print('Example',list(d.items())[:2])\nfor name in ['borrowings','northstar']:\n d=json.loads(pathlib.Path('docs/design/fixtures/'+name+'.json').read_text());print(name, list(d));print(str(d)[:1300])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"26:PHASE_INVENTORY = 'data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P03/phase-entry-inventory.json'\n31:def digest(path):\n38:def _unique_object(pairs):\n42:            raise ValueError('duplicate inventory key: ' + key)\n47:def _inventory(root, relative):\n50:        raise ValueError('inventory path must be repository-relative')\n53:        raise ValueError('inventory must be a nonempty path-to-SHA256 object')\n58:            raise ValueError('invalid inventory entry: ' + name)\n62:def capture_protection(root, historical_path, execution_path, writable=PHASE_FILES,\n69:            inventories.append(_inventory(root, name))\n74:    protected = sorted((set(historical) | set(execution) | set(required_paths)) - set(writable))\n75:    absent = sorted(set(protected) - set(execution))\n77:        errors.append('execution inventory omits protected paths: ' + ', '.join(absent))\n78:    before = {p: digest(root / p) for p in protected}\n80:        'historical_inventory': historical_path,\n81:        'execution_inventory': execution_path,\n82:        'inventory_hashes': {p: digest(root / p) for p in (historical_path,