{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '168,202p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; rg -n 'ExtractionReading|HistoricalFact|AccountingElection|MeasurementEstimate|BehaviourPolicy|FutureInnovation|grouping|likelihood' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; sed -n '30,105p' scripts/check_accounting_p03.py\"","aggregated_output":"add each accepted evidence domain once. Match source observations by exact\ncontext/mapping, never by label similarity. Attach source/assumption IDs to\nconstraints. Branch on finite choices only, with mutually exclusive guards;\ncontinuous families remain formulas. Count completed, infeasible and unresolved\nchoice cells. `ExactWithinScope` requires every cell decided and each matching\nsource obligation resolved or explicitly outside simulation scope. A satisfied\nwitness alone does not establish coverage. Real-world completeness is never\ninferred from this finite result.\n\nSupported solver fragment: rational linear equalities/inequalities, strict\nbounds, finite enums and Boolean combinations lowered to finite disjunctions.\nMoney quantisation either occurs after continuous analysis or uses integer\nminor-unit variables with a separately declared bounded integer solver. Integer\nand nonlinear constraints may not be silently submitted as continuous LPs.\nUnknown-by-unknown products, symbolic discount rates/exponents, arbitrary\nfunctions and unbounded integer search return UnsupportedFragment/Unknown.\nFixed proportions times known totals are linear; variable F,V with F+V=D is\nlinear even when D is rounded. A fixed constraint F/D >= a with known a and\nproved D>0 becomes F>=aD; an unknown a restores bilinearity.\n\nFeasibility results are sat+exact witness, unsat+constraint/source core or\nunknown+reason+undecided formula. Bounds include lower/upper rational value,\nattainment flags, proof/certificate reference, rounding stage and scope. Strict\ninequalities require infimum/supremum semantics. An unbounded result is neither\nunknown nor a finite extreme. Resource budgets are explicit request fields;\ntimeout preserves undecided cells rather than deleting them.\n\n## Temporal selection and local review\n\nAn EvidenceView first filters by availability cutoff and (if requested)\ningestion cutoff. Day-only availability maps to the next local midnight using\nthe named timezone; finer availability requires evidence. Selective explicit\nsupersession removes only the targeted assertions in the same context. A\nsuperseding assertion must be eligible itself. Transitive successors follow\nthe acyclic supersession graph. Competing maximal assertions form a conflict\n229:Uncertainty kinds are ExtractionReading, HistoricalFact, AccountingElection,\n230:MeasurementEstimate, BehaviourPolicy and FutureInnovation. Each has scope,\n235:corrections replace evidence views; likelihoods update probability models;\n240:event probability/likelihood; finite enumeration computes normalised joint\n270:likelihoods list information blocks so totals/components do not duplicate\n\ndef digest(path):\n    try:\n        return hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n    except OSError:\n        return None\n\n\ndef _unique_object(pairs):\n    result = {}\n    for key, value in pairs:\n        if key in result:\n            raise ValueError('duplicate inventory key: ' + key)\n        result[key] = value\n    return result\n\n\ndef _inventory(root, relative):\n    path = Path(relative)\n    if path.is_absolute() or '..' in path.parts or path.as_posix() != relative:\n        raise ValueError('inventory path must be repository-relative')\n    data = json.loads((root / path).read_text(), object_pairs_hook=_unique_object)\n    if not isinstance(data, dict) or not data:\n        raise ValueError('inventory must be a nonempty path-to-SHA256 object')\n    for name, value in data.items():\n        p = Path(name)\n        if (p.is_absolute() or '..' in p.parts or p.as_posix() != name\n                or not isinstance(value, str) or not re.fullmatch('[0-9a-f]{64}', value)):\n            raise ValueError('invalid inventory entry: ' + name)\n    return data\n\n\ndef capture_protection(root, historical_path, execution_path, writable=PHASE_FILES,\n                       required_paths=()):\n    \"\"\"Keep historical differences separate; never replace the execution baseline.\"\"\"\n    errors = []\n    inventories = []\n    for name in (historical_path, execution_path):\n        try:\n            inventories.append(_inventory(root, name))\n        except (OSError, ValueError) as exc:\n            errors.append(f'{name}: {exc}')\n            inventories.append({})\n    historical, execution = inventories\n    protected = sorted((set(historical) | set(execution) | set(required_paths)) - set(writable))\n    absent = sorted(set(protected) - set(execution))\n    if absent:\n        errors.append('execution inventory omits protected paths: ' + ', '.join(absent))\n    before = {p: digest(root / p) for p in protected}\n    return {\n        'historical_inventory': historical_path,\n        'execution_inventory': execution_path,\n        'inventory_hashes': {p: digest(root / p) for p in (historical_path, execution_path)},\n        'excluded_phase_files': list(writable),\n        'errors': errors,\n        'execution_baseline': {p: execution.get(p) for p in protected},\n        'before': before,\n        'missing_before_check': [p for p, h in before.items() if h is None],\n        'changed_since_execution_entry': [p for p in protected if before[p] != execution.get(p)],\n        'historical_differences': [\n            {'path': p, 'phase_entry_sha256': historical[p], 'execution_entry_sha256': execution[p],\n             'attribution': 'Predates this execution, as recorded by the supervisor pre-edit inventory.'}\n            for p in sorted(set(historical) & set(execution) - set(writable))\n            if historical[p] != execution[p]],\n    }\n\n\ndef finish_protection(root, report):\n    report['after'] = {p: digest(root / p) for p in report['before']}\n    report['changed_during_check'] = [p for p in report['before'] if report['before'][p] != report['after'][p]]\n    report['changed_inventory_records'] = [p for p, h in report['inventory_hashes'].items()\n                                           if h is None or digest(root / p) != h]\n    report['passed'] = not any(report[k] for k in (\n        'errors', 'missing_before_check', 'changed_since_execution_entry',\n        'changed_during_check', 'changed_inventory_records'))\n    return report\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
