{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"mkdir -p data/accounting-master/deliverables/P04\ncat > data/accounting-master/deliverables/P04/progress.md <<'EOF'\n# P04 implementation checkpoint\n\nRecovery verified: P04 deliverables, tests and implementation modules were absent.\nThe complete accepted plan and review are the current contract. Z3 4.16.0 and\nPython 3.11.15 are installed. All 384 files in the supervisor phase-entry inventory\nmatch their recorded hashes; that supplied pre-edit inventory is the execution\nbaseline for this first implementation attempt. No GPU or external model is used.\n\nSkeptical audit passed after checking the reviewed repair against P03: named\nalternatives with choice_group=null are conditional predicates, not exhaustive\nchoices. Parent and conditional queries must remain separate. Exact enumeration\nof original inputs and algebra are the comparators; solver success and test counts\ncannot establish accounting validity. Resource exhaustion and unresolved obligations\nprevent exact certification; failed checks trigger local repair.\n\nCurrent changes: this progress checkpoint only.\nNext: add versioned reconstruction profile, fixtures, rational solver,\nreconstruction/adapter, tests and checker. Run P04 tests, P03 regression and the\nP04 checker against the supplied inventory. Both required deliverables remain\nunfinished. Broader MC01–MC35/G1–G18 and human acceptance remain open.\nEOF\ncat > docs/design/spec/reconstruction-profile-v1.md <<'EOF'\n# Bounded reconstruction v1\n\nThis executable profile addresses MC08–MC12, MC18 and MC26. It constructs a joint\nfamily from declared templates, slots, openings, dated mappings and admitted\nobservations. It does not discover templates or infer arbitrary company histories.\n\n## Pre-execution research intent and evidence contract\n\nQuestion: do declared inputs generate the correct family within their finite\nscope? Mechanism: rational linear constraints with shared economic identifiers,\nexplicit finite choices and bounded integer domains. Expected failure modes are\nlost dependence, wrong strict endpoints, unexamined rounding and false completeness.\nComparators are an independent Fraction replay/enumerator over original fixtures\nand analytic continuous bounds. Exact feasible-set equality and endpoint proofs\nare pass criteria. Unsupported operations, unknown backend replies, unfinished\ncells or unresolved matching obligations veto exact certification. Corrupted\ninputs or protection failures veto acceptance and stop the checker. A numerical\nfailure triggers repair, not rejection of the research direction. Runtime is\nexplanatory only. No superiority, general accounting validity, forecast validity,\ncontinuous probabilistic inference or human acceptance follows from these checks.\nConformance JSON and result.md preserve results; progress.md is a reset checkpoint.\n\nSkeptical audit: the earlier ambiguity between named views and search choices is\nresolved explicitly below. Baselines use original inputs, not generated expected\nanswers. Fixture sizes and budgets are engineering choices. No stochastic ranking\nor production-default promotion is attempted. A successful command can still be\nmisleading if both construction and oracle share lowering; the oracle therefore\nreplays postings independently. The integration checks inspect the unnamed\ninterior, not only endpoint extrema.\n\n## Assumptions and defaults\n\n| Choice | Provenance/status | Justification | Failure mode / early diagnostic |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Fraction arithmetic | Core contract, reviewed requirement | exact disclosed decimals | binary-float drift; reject floats |\n| Z3 rational linear solving | existing 4.16.0, implementation hypothesis | exact linear SAT and optimisation | shared backend error; independent enumeration and algebra |\n| finite templates/slots | explicit input, scope hypothesis | tractable reconstruction | omitted histories; preserve exclusions and obligations |\n| budgets | explicit caller input, convenience | bounded execution | premature stop; zero-work and one-cell tests |\n| rounding convention/stage | explicit input, no inferred default | preserve disclosure versus posting semantics | wrong ties; negative/parity fixtures |\n| finite probability measure | explicit joint atoms, hypothesis | dependence and exact Bayes update | overlap/double use; reject duplicate atoms/information |\n| grouping | explicit additive debt profile only | retain contract memory | different resets/maturities/horizon; revalidation tests |\n| deterministic fixtures | engineering comparator | exhaustive small checks | not representative; no empirical forecast claim |\n\n## Family and query semantics\n\nParent P contains opening, slot, transition, mapping and observation constraints.\nNamed view i supplies A_i only. A parent query uses P; a single-view query uses\nP AND A_i. Multiple views require explicit intersection or union. Views may\noverlap or fail to cover P; labels supply neither exclusivity nor probabilities.\nActual finite choices enumerate all declared values jointly. Boolean predicates\nare split by an exhaustive truth-assignment partition of their atomic comparisons;\neach cell includes the formula and its decision prefix. The partition is disjoint\nby construction. Integer variables are enumerated only with finite declared bounds.\nEach candidate assignment/predicate cell is counted once, including infeasible\ncells. Views do not add cells unless their explicit Boolean predicate requires a\nlogical partition. Continuous regions remain symbolic. Unvisited suffixes are\nrepresented by ordinal range and the unchanged family formula.\n\nSlots instantiate nonnegative amounts and an active flag; inactive means zero.\nActive zero is permitted. Both signed posting incidence and economic-state\ncoefficients are declared by the template. Exact context equality is required\nfor observations. One observation ID cannot silently supply incompatible domains.\nUnmatched obligations remain unresolved. Admission records keep six uncertainty\ncategories separate. Stress is conditional, not observed evidence or a likelihood.\n\n## Numerical semantics\n\nFeasibility is checked on each original strict cell before closure optimisation.\nA nonempty convex linear cell has the same infimum/supremum as its closure: for\nany original feasible point x and any closure point y, (1-t)y+t x satisfies every\nstrict inequality for 0<t<=1 and tends to y. The solver therefore optimises closed\ninequalities, proves no better closed value, then tests equality with the endpoint\nunder original constraints. Empty strict cells never acquire relaxation witnesses.\nUnknown in any proof or endpoint test leaves the bound uncertified. Unbounded,\nUnknown, Infeasible and PartialSearch remain distinct. Partial-cell extrema are\nexplored-only, never global certificates.\n\nDebt amounts F,V satisfy F>=0, V>=0, F+V=D. For exact D>0, alpha=F/D is equivalent\nto the fraction parameterisation. With rounded D, use amounts directly. A fixed\nfraction comparison F/D op a may multiply by D only after proving D>0 (or reverse\nthe comparison after proving D<0). Unknown sign or an unknown threshold is\nunsupported. Unknown-by-unknown products and unbounded integer domains are also\nunsupported; they never imply infeasibility.\n\nDisclosure intervals retain inclusion flags. Half-even display domains include\nboth ties for an even displayed minor-unit integer and neither for an odd one.\nPosting quantisation rounds exact rationals at the declared boundary. Symbolic\nposting amounts use bounded integers; continuous relaxation is forbidden.\n\nFinite measures use unique joint atom IDs with weights summing to one. Conditional\nviews are events on atoms. Likelihood information blocks can be used once. Default\nand unresolved mass are retained; unavailable outcomes prevent an unconditional\nmean. Grouping requires matching rate/reset/maturity/hedge keys and additive\ntransition/report checks for the explicit scenario and horizon; contract memory\nis retained. These tests do not prove general aggregation equivalence.\n\n## Execution\n\nUse existing Python/Z3, standard library and accepted P03 dependencies; install\nnothing. Run \"'`python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p '\"'test_accounting_p04.py' -v\"'`\nand the analogous P03 regression, followed by `python3 -B scripts/check_accounting_p04.py\n--output-dir data/accounting-master/deliverables/P04 --execution-inventory\n data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P04/phase-entry-inventory.json`.\nNo accelerator framework is used; CPU-only checks intentionally hide GPU devices.\nThe checker records actual versions, elapsed time, hashes, generated formulas,\nproof queries, observations and protection comparisons. Git is unavailable; content\nhashes preserve provenance. Human acceptance remains pending.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
